From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: DrummingBird1 <1979036+DrummingBird1@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 16:16:11 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] D3D12: say at startup where the shader cache is and whether
 draws wait

One line in the run log, "[D3D12] shader cache: <dir>; a draw whose
shader is compiling is waited for | skipped (D3D12_SHADER_ASYNC)", so a
log shows which mode a run used. The launcher sets the switch, and its
run log does not record the environment.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 libs/video/rsx_d3d12_backend.c | 4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/libs/video/rsx_d3d12_backend.c b/libs/video/rsx_d3d12_backend.c
index a39b3442..463024cf 100644
--- a/libs/video/rsx_d3d12_backend.c
+++ b/libs/video/rsx_d3d12_backend.c
@@ -2351,7 +2351,9 @@ static const char* shader_cache_dir(void)
             printf("[D3D12] shader cache %s unavailable, compiling every time\n", dir);
             dir[0] = 0;
         }
-        if (dir[0]) printf("[D3D12] shader cache: %s\n", dir);
+        { const char* a = getenv("D3D12_SHADER_ASYNC");
+          printf("[D3D12] shader cache: %s; a draw whose shader is compiling is %s\n", dir[0] ? dir : "off",
+                 (a && a[0] == '1') ? "skipped (D3D12_SHADER_ASYNC)" : "waited for"); }
     }
     return dir[0] ? dir : NULL;
 }
